 ## How to use
 
 Use the exact recorded prompt and the displayed original reference assets in order. Changes to the prompt or inputs create an untested variant.
 
+Upload the original synthetic room photo first and the separate red-circle markup overlay second. The overlay identifies the vase; it is not the generated result. The recorded working prompt is in Chinese and remains unchanged here. An English translation would be a new, untested prompt.
+
 ## Observed result
 
 Vase changed from cream to cobalt blue, red markup removed. Jug, dried stems, tiles and window remain visually consistent; new glaze is glossier.
 
+## Generation evidence and limits
+
+The [run record](https://github.com/picontapLab/prompt-seen/blob/89395feb8e5fda7419aa3f5d2594df8a71fb3363/content/examples/x_282/run.yaml) links the prompt hash to inputs a_373 and a_374, in that order, and output a_372. The [generation receipt](https://github.com/picontapLab/prompt-seen/blob/89395feb8e5fda7419aa3f5d2594df8a71fb3363/production/gpt-image-26-2026-11/audit/S10.json) preserves input and output hashes. Its timestamp is November 5 UTC, corresponding to November 4 in Los Angeles, the date displayed for this run.
+
+GPT Image 2.6 is the [project owner's version attribution](https://github.com/picontapLab/prompt-seen/blob/89395feb8e5fda7419aa3f5d2594df8a71fb3363/production/model-version-annotation-2026-11-05.json). The tool returned no exact API model ID; seed, sampling and quality settings were not recorded. This one output shows a color change with a glossier surface, not proof that a color edit preserves every reflection or pixel. Check material finish and surrounding objects when trying your own image.
+
 ## Source and generation
 
 The source provides an original prompt; this production uses the separately recorded working prompt. [Source](https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/image-prompting#guide-an-edit-with-markup). Source-post engagement does not measure this newly generated example.
